From: ASK maintainers <ask@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] moal: own cfg80211 scans through admission, completion and teardown

Give cached and firmware scans a separate cfg80211 owner and a generation.
Serialize every completion, stamp queued reports at receipt, and drain the
old timer before rearming it. Complete real timeouts even when hang recovery
is suppressed, and stop delayed work before destroying its queue. Keep
fallible request preparation before ownership transfer and return success
once the driver has accepted (and possibly already completed) a request.

Serialize release of the firmware scan semaphore too: cancellation, a scan
report and cleanup may race to release the same acquisition. Preserve ACS's
existing non-aborted completion behavior.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
